{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/breakdown_art/status/2105192577850806751","id":"2105192577850806751","text":"I am happy to share the results of my first serious attempt at training a model based on the insane Marigold V2 by @AntonObukhov1 and his team! \n\nAI generated depth of field has been historically unusable, lacking detail and temporal coherence. \nMarigoldV2 solved the detail part and I set out to solve the coherence. \n\nThrough a series of targeted training passes focusing on large scale morphing and flicker first, I then moved to boundary and edge detection before finally squeezing back in the detail using Marigold V2s Sink Loss technique\n\nThe end result speaks for itself and while still not perfect, I have learned tons and have set out to expand my personal library of high quality CGI, photoreal scenes so I can do a much larger training run in future. \n\nTraining was completed over 400 H200 Hours.","raw_text":{"text":"I am happy to share the results of my first serious attempt at training a model based on the insane Marigold V2 by @AntonObukhov1 and his team! \n\nAI generated depth of field has been historically unusable, lacking detail and temporal coherence. \nMarigoldV2 solved the detail part and I set out to solve the coherence. \n\nThrough a series of targeted training passes focusing on large scale morphing and flicker first, I then moved to boundary and edge detection before finally squeezing back in the detail using Marigold V2s Sink Loss technique\n\nThe end result speaks for itself and while still not perfect, I have learned tons and have set out to expand my personal library of high quality CGI, photoreal scenes so I can do a much larger training run in future. \n\nTraining was completed over 400 H200 Hours.","display_text_range":[0,807],"facets":[{"type":"mention","indices":[115,129],"original":"AntonObukhov1","id":"1257961662331707392"},{"type":"media","indices":[280,303],"id":"2105191464934461440","display":"pic.